Overlay patch 0019: the iOS menu suite in Starship's menubar (SYNC WAVE 1;
reference 0017/0018 shapes adapted to this port's UIWidgets menu framework).
- Settings -> iOS submenu: Touch Controls (Double-Tap Z to Lock — default
  OFF per the Starship judgement call, D8; Haptics; Opacity; Left-Handed;
  Stick Response; Customize Layout...), Display (Max Frame Rate 60/120,
  Performance HUD), Menu (Menu Scale, LIVE), Advanced (Remote Console).
- LIVE menu scale: per-frame ratio-apply of gSohIos.MenuScale against the
  boot value LUS applied at Gui init (overlay 0010) — bootstrap-on-first-
  frame, so no LUS revision is needed.
- Mouse-free swipe-scroll: each top-level menubar dropdown consumes the
  shell's queued deltas (SohIos_TakeMenuScrollFor, overlay 0014 rev2) when
  the finger is horizontally inside it — SetScrollY on the popup window
  itself (Starship's dropdowns are plain ImGui windows; no internals).
- iOS quit: menu Quit freezes with Close() alone (no desktop loop to
  unwind) -> CVarSave + exit(0) (reference batch-4 root cause).

--- a/src/port/ui/ImguiUI.cpp
+++ b/src/port/ui/ImguiUI.cpp
@@ -230,8 +230,50 @@
     ImGui::SetCursorScreenPos(ImVec2(canvasPos.x, canvasPos.y + canvasSize.y + 10));
 }
 
+#ifdef __IOS__
+// SOH_IOS (overlay 0019): shell-contract helpers for the phone UI.
+#include <cmath>
+extern "C" float SohIos_TakeMenuScrollFor(float winX, float winW);
+
+// Finger swipes queued by the shell (overlay 0014 rev2) scroll the menu
+// dropdown under the finger. Mouse-free: no hover tooltips, no slider
+// side-effects (reference device feedback).
+static void SohIosUi_ApplyMenuScroll() {
+    float dy = SohIos_TakeMenuScrollFor(ImGui::GetWindowPos().x, ImGui::GetWindowSize().x);
+    if (dy != 0.0f) {
+        ImGui::SetScrollY(ImGui::GetScrollY() - dy);
+    }
+}
+
+// LIVE menu scale: LUS applied gSohIos.MenuScale once at Gui init (overlay
+// 0010). Track the applied value — bootstrapped from the CVar on the first
+// frame, before the slider can move — and ratio-scale the live ImGui style
+// whenever it changes. FontGlobalScale is absolute; style paddings scale by
+// ratio (the Ship of Harkinian port ScaleImGui approach).
+static void SohIosUi_MenuScaleLive() {
+    static float sohIosApplied = 0.0f;
+    float want = CVarGetFloat("gSohIos.MenuScale", 0.85f);
+    want = want < 0.6f ? 0.6f : (want > 1.2f ? 1.2f : want);
+    if (sohIosApplied == 0.0f) {
+        sohIosApplied = want; // boot value: already applied at Gui init
+        return;
+    }
+    if (fabsf(want - sohIosApplied) > 0.001f) {
+        ImGui::GetStyle().ScaleAllSizes(want / sohIosApplied);
+        ImGui::GetIO().FontGlobalScale = want;
+        sohIosApplied = want;
+    }
+}
+#endif
